  "content": {
    "text": "S&P 500, Nasdaq And Dow End Holiday-Shortened Week Higher As Investors Cheer US-Iran Peace Deal — SPCX, AMZN, ONDS, NFLX, TTWO In Focus\n-\nThe S&P 500 and the Nasdaq 100 rose 1.1% and 2.5%, respectively, while the Dow Jones added 0.1%.\n-\nIntel stock soared as President Donald Trump said the firm will work alongside Apple Inc. to design and produce semiconductors.\n-\nBoth WTI and Brent futures were trading at less than $80 per barrel at the time of writing.\nU.S. stock indices gained on Thursday as optimism around a US-Iran peace deal offset investor concern of a rate hike following the U.S. Federal Reserve's monetary policy in the previous session, while a rally in Intel shares supported the Nasdaq.\nThe S&P 500 jumped 1.1%, Nasdaq rose 2.5% and the Dow Jones added 0.1%. The Russell 2000, which tracks stocks with small market capitalizations, rose 2%.\nAmong ETFs tracking benchmark indexes, the SPDR S&P 500 ETF (SPY) gained 1.2%, and Invesco QQQ Trust (QQQ) ended Thursday around 2.5% higher, while the SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (DIA) ended 0.3% higher.\nMeanwhile, the VanEck Semiconductor ETF (SMH) soared 6%.\nHowever, retail sentiment on Stocktwits for SPY, QQQ, and DIA was 'bullish', with 'normal' to 'high' message volumes.\nUS Market Drivers\nThe technology sector jumped about 3%, powered by a 10.6% jump in Intel shares (INTC) after U.S. President Donald Trump said that Apple Inc. (AAPL) had agreed to use Intel's foundry services. The development marks a major win for the government-backed chipmaker and appears to confirm months of deal speculation.\nRobert Conzo, chief executive officer at The Wealth Alliance, told CNBC in an interview that he believes there's \"more bullishness around companies working together because of [artificial intelligence] infrastructure and the effects of AI within many, many different competing industries.\" He also said, \"I think Apple-Intel was a little proxy for what you could see happening in the future.\"\nOil prices also dipped, with Brent and WTI futures trading below $80 per barrel, supported by a US-Iran peace deal.\nDonald Trump and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian signed a preliminary agreement on Wednesday in a bid to end the conflict between the two countries and reopen the Strait of Hormuz, a move that could increase global oil supplies.\nAs part of the deal, the U.S. will begin lifting its naval blockade of Iran and restore pre-war military deployments within 30 days. Iran, in turn, will facilitate the reopening of the Strait of Hormuz, allowing commercial shipping to resume without transit fees. The deal outlined a 60-day negotiation period, which can be extended, to finalize a broader settlement.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "S&P 500, Nasdaq And Dow End Holiday-Shortened Week Higher As Investors Cheer US-Iran Peace Deal — SPCX, AMZN, ONDS, NFLX, TTWO In Focus",
      "-",
      "The S&P 500 and the Nasdaq 100 rose 1.1% and 2.5%, respectively, while the Dow Jones added 0.1%.",
      "-",
      "Intel stock soared as President Donald Trump said the firm will work alongside Apple Inc. to design and produce semiconductors.",
      "-",
      "Both WTI and Brent futures were trading at less than $80 per barrel at the time of writing.",
      "U.S. stock indices gained on Thursday as optimism around a US-Iran peace deal offset investor concern of a rate hike following the U.S. Federal Reserve's monetary policy in the previous session, while a rally in Intel shares supported the Nasdaq.",
      "The S&P 500 jumped 1.1%, Nasdaq rose 2.5% and the Dow Jones added 0.1%. The Russell 2000, which tracks stocks with small market capitalizations, rose 2%.",
      "Among ETFs tracking benchmark indexes, the SPDR S&P 500 ETF (SPY) gained 1.2%, and Invesco QQQ Trust (QQQ) ended Thursday around 2.5% higher, while the SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (DIA) ended 0.3% higher.",
      "Meanwhile, the VanEck Semiconductor ETF (SMH) soared 6%.",
      "However, retail sentiment on Stocktwits for SPY, QQQ, and DIA was 'bullish', with 'normal' to 'high' message volumes.",
      "US Market Drivers",
      "The technology sector jumped about 3%, powered by a 10.6% jump in Intel shares (INTC) after U.S. President Donald Trump said that Apple Inc. (AAPL) had agreed to use Intel's foundry services. The development marks a major win for the government-backed chipmaker and appears to confirm months of deal speculation.",
      "Robert Conzo, chief executive officer at The Wealth Alliance, told CNBC in an interview that he believes there's \"more bullishness around companies working together because of [artificial intelligence] infrastructure and the effects of AI within many, many different competing industries.\" He also said, \"I think Apple-Intel was a little proxy for what you could see happening in the future.\"",
      "Oil prices also dipped, with Brent and WTI futures trading below $80 per barrel, supported by a US-Iran peace deal.",
      "Donald Trump and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian signed a preliminary agreement on Wednesday in a bid to end the conflict between the two countries and reopen the Strait of Hormuz, a move that could increase global oil supplies.",
      "As part of the deal, the U.S. will begin lifting its naval blockade of Iran and restore pre-war military deployments within 30 days. Iran, in turn, will facilitate the reopening of the Strait of Hormuz, allowing commercial shipping to resume without transit fees. The deal outlined a 60-day negotiation period, which can be extended, to finalize a broader settlement."
